      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`DFlashDraftInputV2.prepare_for_decode` writes the committed, current and next KV lengths with one CPU-tensor `__setitem__` per request and field, i.e. 3 x bs element writes every decode step. On DSV4.1-Flash GB300 disagg DEP16 (40 running per rank), `prepare_for_decode` takes 1.0-1.4 ms per step, and these element writes are about 0.4 ms of it. That time sits on the pre-agreement host path of the last DP rank to arrive.\n\n## Related PRs\n\nOne of four DSV4.1 attn-DP decode host-path changes that cut the host work between the DP agreement and the draft graph launch. They are independent in code and were measured together: #47676 (padded metadata glue), #47677 (persistent DP-MoE counts), #47678 (bulk decode-prep fill) and #47685 (KV page top-up, measured on top of the other three).\n\n## Modifications\n\nThe per-element loop is replaced by an exact rewrite, so there is no switch:\n- The committed lengths and top-k values are gathered into lists.\n- Each length buffer is written once through its numpy view. The buffers, their dtypes and the point at which they are written, before the non-blocking H2D copies, are unchanged.\n- The sums, max top-k and uniform top-k value are computed from the lists.\n\nAll runs: GB300, DSV4.1-Flash, on a 2026-10-30 nightly.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- GSM8K, 1P1D DEP16 with real DSpark acceptance, together with the two sibling host changes (#47676, #47677): 96.82% vs 96.89%; accept length 3.50 vs 3.49-3.51.\n- TP4 c1 agg (mega flag on): T=1 GSM8K 97.33% vs 97.33%, long-context needle retrieval at 20K-160K tokens 48/48 vs 48/48 (greedy) and 24/24 vs 24/24 (T=1), accept length 3.591 vs 3.598.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\n| | DEP16 nsys, before | DEP16 nsys, after |\n|---|---|---|\n| `prepare_for_decode` NVTX range, median over ranks | 1162 us | 774 us |\n\nCombined DEP32 / DEP16 / TP4 numbers: see #47676. They come from the same runs, and those numbers are **combined** across the three changes.\n\nThe teardown note from that PR applies here as well: a MegaMoE NVLink barrier timeout after the benchmark abort also occurs without these changes; serving-phase results are unaffected.\n\n## Checklist\n- [x] Format with pre-commit\n- [x] GPU validation on cluster (above)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41821589951](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41821589951)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41821589332](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41821589332)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41821589526](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41821589526)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
